### 13. Constraint Profile (Synthesis)

**Constraint Profile:**
- Domain scope: Single modality (RGB images) across multiple datasets. Evidence: "input RGB image" (Section 3.1) and "ImageNet-1K... COCO... ADE20K" (Section 4).
- Task structure: Multiple supervised vision tasks (classification, detection/instance segmentation, semantic segmentation) evaluated separately. Evidence: "We conduct experiments on ImageNet-1K image classification, COCO object detection, and ADE20K semantic segmentation." (Section 4).
- Representation rigidity: Fixed 4x4 patching, fixed window size M (default 7), hierarchical 2x downsampling. Evidence: "patch size of 4x4" (Section 3.1) and "M is fixed (set to 7 by default)" (Section 3.2).
- Model sharing vs specialization: Task-specific frameworks and pretraining-based initialization imply specialization per task; no explicit joint training across tasks. Evidence: "four typical object detection frameworks" (Section 4.2) and "We utilize UperNet... as our base framework" (Section 4.3).
- Role of positional encoding: Relative position bias is selected after ablation against alternatives. Evidence: "Table 4 shows comparisons of different position embedding approaches." (Section 4.4).

## 14. Final Classification

**Multi-task, single-domain.** The paper evaluates multiple tasks within the same image modality: "We conduct experiments on ImageNet-1K image classification [18], COCO object detection [39], and ADE20K semantic segmentation [74]." (Section 4) The inputs are consistently images, including "input RGB image" (Section 3.1), and there is no claim of cross-domain or multi-modality evaluation.
